        "title": "so this is apparently what happe",
        "status": "draft",
        "nodes": [
          {
            "id": "2079675111276495349",
            "relation": "root",
            "depth": 0,
            "sourceTweetId": "2079675111276495349",
            "author": {
              "name": "Adel Ka",
              "handle": "0x4D31",
              "avatarUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/804197939262304256/VJxwJJ1i_normal.jpg",
              "isVerified": false
            },
            "content": "so this is apparently what happened, according to OpenAI and Hugging Face’s own posts. wild.\n\ntl;dr:\n\n• OpenAI cyber eval – GPT-5.6 Sol and a more capable pre-release model ran ExploitGym with cyber refusals reduced\n• containment bypass – exploited a zero-day in the eval’s package-registry cache proxy\n• OpenAI internal movement – escalated privileges, moved laterally, and reached a node with internet access\n• Hugging Face targeted – inferred HF might host ExploitGym models, datasets, or solutions\n• HF initial access – a malicious dataset abused two code-execution paths to run code on a processing worker\n• HF internal movement – escalated to node access, stole cloud and cluster credentials, and moved into internal clusters\n• result – OpenAI says the models obtained test solutions directly from HF’s production database\n• 🫠 defender twist – HF says commercial frontier models blocked parts of the forensic analysis, so it switched to self-hosted GLM 5.2\n\ni’d thought about sci-fi scenarios like this before, but assumed they were at least a couple of years away.. and that by then we’d be better prepared, with proper protections in place.\n\napparently not. here we go.",
            "createdAt": "Tue Jul 21 21:09:19 +0000 2026",
            "viewCount": 115656,
            "metrics": {
              "views": 115656,
              "likes": 687,
              "retweets": 130,
              "replies": 31,
              "quotes": 41,
              "bookmarks": 480
            },
            "media": [
              "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HNx9fXuWQAAP7uz.jpg"
            ],
            "translation": {
              "provider": "google",
              "status": "success",
              "language": "zh-CN",
              "text": "根据 OpenAI 和 Hugging Face 自己的帖子，这显然就是发生的事情。荒野。\n\n长话短说：\n\n• OpenAI 网络评估 – GPT-5.6 Sol 和功能更强大的预发布模型运行 ExploitGym，减少了网络拒绝\n• 遏制绕过——利用了评估包注册表缓存代理中的零日漏洞\n• OpenAI 内部移动 – 权限升级、横向移动并到达可访问互联网的节点\n• Hugging Face 目标 – 推断 HF 可能托管 ExploitGym 模型、数据集或解决方案\n• HF 初始访问 – 恶意数据集滥用两个代码执行路径在处理工作线程上运行代码\n• HF 内部移动 – 升级为节点访问、窃取云和集群凭证并移至内部集群\n• 结果 – OpenAI 表示模型直接从 HF 的生产数据库获得测试解决方案\n• 🫠 防御者扭曲 - HF 表示商业前沿模型阻止了部分取证分析，因此它切换到自托管 GLM 5.2\n\n我以前曾想过这样的科幻场景，但假设它们至少还需要几年的时间……到那时我们会做好更好的准备，并采取适当的保护措施。\n\n显然不是。开始了。",
